  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "hs_note",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -420
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "HAND SPARKS\n\nHold your hands up to the camera and wave them: they throw sparks. The faster you move, the more sparks fly; hold still and the glow dies away.\n\nFlip the switch on the left and let Floret use your camera. Your hands show as faint dots, so you can see what the sparks follow.\n\nHow it works: each frame the patch measures how far the dots have travelled since the frame before (it remembers them in a Write / Read pair), averages that into one speed, and turns the speed into how many sparks to release. A tiny amount of movement is ignored so a resting hand stays quiet.\n\nTry: change the Emitter's colours, the World's gravity (negative lifts the sparks up) or the Turbulence strength for wilder drift.",
        "width": 600,
        "height": 330
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "HAND SPARKS\n\nHold your hands up to the camera and wave them: they throw sparks. The faster you move, the more sparks fly; hold still and the glow dies away.\n\nFlip the switch on the left and let Floret use your camera. Your hands show as faint dots, so you can see what the sparks follow.\n\nHow it works: each frame the patch measures how far the dots have travelled since the frame before (it remembers them in a Write / Read pair), averages that into one speed, and turns the speed into how many sparks to release. A tiny amount of movement is ignored so a resting hand stays quiet.\n\nTry: change the Emitter's colours, the World's gravity (negative lifts the sparks up) or the Turbulence strength for wilder drift.",
        "width": 600,
        "height": 330
      }
    },
